Remediates the shadow-credentials finding in key-admins-domain-root-rights.json, per Raymond's
explicit decision: remove bhound from Key Admins and disable the account.

Command: Remove-ADGroupMember -Identity "Key Admins" -Members bhound -Confirm:$false
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1
}

-Confirm:$false added proactively, applying the ConfirmImpact lesson from this same exercise's
AdSyncConfig stall: Remove-ADGroupMember prompts for confirmation by default under AD DS
cmdlets' normal ConfirmImpact, and qm guest exec has no console for a prompt to reach. Worked
clean on the first attempt as a result — no stall this time.

Command: Disable-ADAccount -Identity bhound
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1
}

Command: Get-ADUser bhound -Properties Enabled,MemberOf | Select Enabled,MemberOf
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1,
   "out-data" : "\r\nEnabled MemberOf\r\n------- --------\r\n  False {}      \r\n\r\n\r\n"
}

RESULT: bhound is Enabled: False, MemberOf: {} (empty — confirms the Key Admins removal landed,
not just the group-remove command's exit code). The domain-wide msDS-KeyCredentialLink write
path this account held is closed. This also resolves one of report.md's outstanding Open
questions ("bhound's fate is still undecided") — decided and executed same day, disable chosen
over UPN-fix or sync-exclusion, which also moots the earlier open question about whether
bhound's Entra Connect export would fail on its computed bhound@district.local UPN, since the
account will no longer sync as enabled.
